03:44:20,280 --> 03:44:20,980
Yeah, right?

3256
03:44:21,340 --> 03:44:22,240
I thought so too.

3257
03:44:23,470 --> 03:44:27,610
Unfortunately, you know, I just wasn't a big fan of the actual game in the game.

3258
03:44:30,680 --> 03:44:35,700
And when I saw the references... I don't want to spoil too much, of course, but you know what I mean when I say references.

3259
03:44:36,600 --> 03:44:41,100
I just knew it was going to be the same type of puzzles just within those domains.

3260
03:44:41,620 --> 03:44:43,440
And I was like, I don't want to do that.

3261
03:44:43,560 --> 03:44:44,920
That does not excite me.

3262
03:44:45,040 --> 03:44:45,320
I'm sorry.

3263
03:44:46,780 --> 03:44:47,300
You know?

3264
03:44:49,080 --> 03:44:49,660
At all.

3265
03:44:52,260 --> 03:44:56,900
Like, it's just going to be high school questions in physics and stuff like that.

3266
03:44:56,980 --> 03:44:58,720
And that's not a fun puzzle to me.

3267
03:45:06,110 --> 03:45:09,410
We should try Polybridge, but that maybe feels like more a stream game.

3268
03:45:10,910 --> 03:45:12,350
Hey, that would be a good one, maybe.

3269
03:45:15,190 --> 03:45:17,210
That could be an idea for sure.

3270
03:45:20,030 --> 03:45:22,170
What have you not liked about Create so far?

3271
03:45:22,470 --> 03:45:27,750
The thing I don't like about Create... is that I think sometimes it is...

3272
03:45:30,960 --> 03:45:32,000
Very confusing.

3273
03:45:33,000 --> 03:45:35,240
But that could just be a me problem.

3274
03:45:35,400 --> 03:45:37,780
I feel like some of the mechanics are not super intuitive.

3275
03:45:38,420 --> 03:45:39,920
Especially the packaging stuff.

3276
03:45:45,110 --> 03:45:55,150
I don't like how there's something called a packager, how there's like this stock link thing and the stock ticker or whatever, like all these weird things.

3277
03:45:55,730 --> 03:45:59,390
It seems to me like you could reduce all that complexity significantly.

3278
03:46:00,790 --> 03:46:04,910
For example, at the end there, why do I need to have a packager for this thing to go in?

3279
03:46:05,230 --> 03:46:07,310
You know, for example, that makes no sense to me.

3280
03:46:07,950 --> 03:46:11,830
Let the package go in there and just have the vault do that thing, you know what I mean?

3281
03:46:17,900 --> 03:46:20,360
It just feels like there's unnecessary complexity.

3282
03:46:20,640 --> 03:46:22,620
That's my only complaint, I would say.

3283
03:46:23,800 --> 03:46:28,960
But obviously, when you learn the complexities, then you understand it, and then you can play with it, you know?

3284
03:46:29,320 --> 03:46:32,960
This is just about the time when you're learning it to the point where you have the understanding.

3285
03:46:37,980 --> 03:46:42,900
I mean, yeah, it may just be because I'm not seeing the logic yet.

3286
03:46:45,300 --> 03:46:47,820
Like, when you have the full picture, you know, everything makes sense, of course.

3287
03:46:52,980 --> 03:46:53,520
Anything else?

3288
03:46:53,580 --> 03:46:55,540
Let me think what else I don't like about Create.

3289
03:46:59,870 --> 03:47:01,690
Honestly, there's very little I don't like.

3290
03:47:02,110 --> 03:47:07,950
It's a free mod, and it oozes quality in every single place, you know?

3291
03:47:09,110 --> 03:47:12,870
It is honestly probably the best mod I have ever played for a game.

3292
03:47:14,370 --> 03:47:19,350
It is unbelievable how much work and effort and love went into this.

3293
03:47:19,950 --> 03:47:21,930
Just the design of the blocks, you know?

3294
03:47:22,250 --> 03:47:24,350
They feel like they could come out of vanilla.

3295
03:47:25,770 --> 03:47:26,770
It's beautiful.

3296
03:47:28,670 --> 03:47:30,950
Hats off to the people who made this, man.

3297
03:47:38,120 --> 03:47:40,180
Like, the quality is next level.

3298
03:47:42,060 --> 03:47:43,440
Take on the extender grip.

3299
03:47:43,500 --> 03:47:43,980
I love it.

3300
03:47:44,620 --> 03:47:46,640
It does feel slightly janky.

3301
03:47:47,060 --> 03:47:47,540
You know?

3302
03:47:49,820 --> 03:47:50,340
Slightly.

3303
03:47:50,800 --> 03:47:53,100
But, like, just the way the animations work and stuff.

3304
03:47:53,920 --> 03:47:56,240
But, all in all, I like it.

3305
03:47:58,140 --> 03:47:58,880
It's great.

3306
03:48:09,010 --> 03:48:10,790
It's insane how those mods are free, right?

3307
03:48:12,330 --> 03:48:13,290
I mean, they should be free.

3308
03:48:13,370 --> 03:48:14,330
That's the whole point of mods.

3309
03:48:15,030 --> 03:48:16,910
It's just wild how much effort went into it, you know?

3310
03:48:17,010 --> 03:48:18,250
It's just so much quality.

3311
03:48:20,250 --> 03:48:21,350
I don't like paid mods.

3312
03:48:22,950 --> 03:48:23,830
Then they're not mods.

3313
03:48:27,010 --> 03:48:28,130
It's just kind of weird.

3314
03:48:28,490 --> 03:48:29,430
Sometimes I do it, though.

3315
03:48:29,630 --> 03:48:30,950
Like, I did it for KSP, right?

3316
03:48:31,050 --> 03:48:34,150
But I don't understand why that is paid, to be honest.

3317
03:48:34,250 --> 03:48:36,870
That one mod feels weird.

3318
03:48:37,190 --> 03:48:39,170
It's like that one guy, the really weird dude.

3319
03:48:39,210 --> 03:48:40,170
I don't know if you saw the news.

3320
03:48:40,770 --> 03:48:46,670
There was a guy who made a mod for... I guess it was various games for VR.

3321
03:48:47,790 --> 03:48:51,390
And then I think it was for Cyberpunk, among others.

3322
03:48:53,010 --> 03:48:58,710
And then CDPR told them, hey, it's cool that you make mods, but can you not, you know, charge for it?

3323
03:48:58,990 --> 03:48:59,630
Just make it free.

3324
03:48:59,770 --> 03:49:00,450
It's fine that you make them.

3325
03:49:00,510 --> 03:49:01,190
Just make it free.

3326
03:49:01,470 --> 03:49:04,610
You can still take donations if people want to do that, but just make it free.

3327
03:49:05,370 --> 03:49:08,530
And he threw a hissy fit, you know, and deleted all the mods so nobody could play them.

3328
03:49:09,950 --> 03:49:10,590
That's crazy.

3329
03:49:14,750 --> 03:49:18,270
Paid mods equals DLC like... Yeah, I don't know.

3330
03:49:18,450 --> 03:49:22,290
I feel like that should be an official collaboration with the developers then or something.

3331
03:49:22,450 --> 03:49:22,770
I don't know.

3332
03:49:25,010 --> 03:49:27,450
Will they do magic mods or bigger modpack?

3333
03:49:27,710 --> 03:49:28,170
No.

3334
03:49:28,950 --> 03:49:31,130
This series is just create.

3335
03:49:37,260 --> 03:49:37,600
Yeah.

3336
03:49:37,600 --> 03:49:44,140
But I did say, like, I think in the future, like far future, maybe like a couple years from now or so, that's very loosely said, though.

3337
03:49:44,200 --> 03:49:45,720
It could be less, could be more, I don't know.

3338
03:49:46,600 --> 03:49:51,260
But I do want to do this crazy thing where we just add a shit ton of everything.

3339
03:49:51,420 --> 03:49:53,780
You know, everybody says, I want that mod added.

3340
03:49:54,580 --> 03:50:02,940
Like, everybody gets their say, you know, unless, of course, it's TOS breaking, and we just make the most bad shit insane mod pack that makes no sense.

3341
03:50:04,280 --> 03:50:04,720
Guns?

3342
03:50:04,880 --> 03:50:05,100
Sure.

3343
03:50:05,780 --> 03:50:06,580
Atomic weapons?

3344
03:50:06,780 --> 03:50:07,340
If it exists?

3345
03:50:07,500 --> 03:50:07,700
Sure.

3346
03:50:07,840 --> 03:50:08,120
Add it.

3347
03:50:08,780 --> 03:50:09,580
You know, like, everything.

3348
03:50:10,600 --> 03:50:11,620
You'd get so overwhelmed.

3349
03:50:11,620 --> 03:50:12,200
That's the point.

3350
03:50:12,480 --> 03:50:12,880
You know?

3351
03:50:13,400 --> 03:50:15,460
It's just gonna be absolute bonkers.

3352
03:50:16,440 --> 03:50:17,900
Everybody gets to add a mod.

3353
03:50:20,040 --> 03:50:21,540
Assuming the game doesn't crash.

3354
